## Session 5 ledger

**Seven structural fixes landed and validated** (tree `72677E1A` = 0.11.17, all knobs runtime-writable):
1. **make_durable reverted to passive settle** — reproduced the known-good AB52387F srcversion byte-exactly, clearing sess4's cross-node D-state wedge.
2. **Bounded publish batch (5s, self-freeing workers)** — broke the measured cross-node bast-worker deadlock (publish drain remote-waiting 470s on a peer-held cluster while its own AG release sat queued behind it; proven end-to-end with stacks + P-WAIT-EXTEND + P12 on live nodes).
3. **Eager-demote publish** — routed children flush-to-platter at publish instead of claiming contended clusters; kills the pop-then-fail claim hole behind the cwr `exp=""` stale-read class.
4. **Wave A pre-pass** (batch writeback + single log force) — per-child handoff cost 5-9ms → <1ms (P138-proven); **dir_reuse back in budget at 116/120s**.
5. **Orphan-reclaim default-on with gate v3** + demoter forensics (which disproved two leak theories by naming live dwork demotes).
6. **caw_unlock_backoff default-on** — fixes the measured orphaned-slot-bit convoy (unlock CAS losing 100 retries to waiter churn).
7. **P15-ORPH-PROCEED (CAW, 250ms-persistent)** — replaced the per-handoff 3-second starve-force tax that made 8-node dir races convoy 100-220s. GPT (RULE 5) confirmed the abort was circular; the no-qualifier first cut stole undiscovered CAS wins (fairness starvation) and was corrected with the resource-scoped persistence clock.

**Result: cache_coherency@8 green (13-15s, 765/765) on three consecutive fresh-prep boards** — it had never passed in the board slot this session. Rows 1-9 + 20 all green with fio at 141% of native.

**Open front: dlm_fairness@8** — the sole red row (rows 11-19 are its pre-assert victims). The end-of-session A/B matrix (in state.md) excludes every individual knob, VM state, and warm/cold ordering; next session's decisive experiment is specified: instrument where fairness's 30s goes and A/B `pub_eager_demote` off — the old claim-path semantics are now safe to test since the bounded batch neutralized the original deadlock. After fairness: full board on one build → 16 → 32 → cawp/tcp/caw ladders → matrix green → marker.

